### 2. `EntityDeathEvent` — killer check + spawner exclusion

**Simple killer check:** `D:\.1 Work Stations\RootMC\Plugin Building\Minecraft\plugins\root-economy\src\main\java\com\rootrecord\minecraft\rootessentials\listener\GoldFoundListener.java`

```132:149:D:\.1 Work Stations\RootMC\Plugin Building\Minecraft\plugins\root-economy\src\main\java\com\rootrecord\minecraft\rootessentials\listener\GoldFoundListener.java
    @EventHandler(priority = EventPriority.MONITOR, ignoreCancelled = true)
    public void onEntityDeath(EntityDeathEvent event) {
        Player killer = event.getEntity().getKiller();
        if (killer == null || skipPlayer(killer)) {
            return;
        }
        // ... process drops
    }
```

